With the installation of new tools on the app servers within the Stratos Datacenter, certain functionalities now necessitate graphical user interface (GUI) access.
Adjust the default runlevel on all App servers in Stratos Datacenter to enable GUI booting by default. 
It's imperative not to initiate a server reboot after completing this task.

SOLUTION
To configure the App servers to boot into the GUI by default without rebooting, you will use systemctl set-default. This command updates the system's default boot target configuration for the next boot, while leaving your current running session untouched.

🖥️ Configuration Command
Execute the following command on each App server in the Stratos Datacenter:

bash
sudo systemctl set-default graphical.target
🔍 Verification
After running the command, you can verify that the default target has been successfully changed:

bash
systemctl get-default
You should see the following output, confirming that the system is now configured to boot into the GUI:

text
graphical.target
📝 Important Notes
No Reboot Required: Using set-default only modifies the symbolic link for the next boot. It does not switch the currently running system or require an immediate reboot .

Live Session: To start the GUI in your current session (without changing the boot default), you would typically use sudo systemctl isolate graphical.target . However, since the task specifically requires changing the default boot configuration and forbids rebooting, set-default is the correct and sufficient command.

